# Go sources are LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, so without this a Windows
# checkout rewrites every .go file to CRLF. gofmt treats CRLF as unformatted, so
# the format gate then fails on all files at once and the rest of the job never
# runs -- which is exactly what happened on this repository's first Windows run.
*.go text eol=lf

# Channel and journal files are append-only records written byte-for-byte by
# several different writers, including a native binary that appends a single "\n"
# terminated line per record. Line-ending translation would rewrite bytes that a
# content-addressed id was computed over, so git must leave them exactly alone.
*.jsonl -text
